{%- comment -%}
  Black Friday countdown banner.

  Macarena's brief (4 Nov 2026): "el banner de water for good (pero black
  friday) y el count down en vez del conteo de dolares y el call to action que
  sign up to the newsletter/sms".

  So this is the Water For Good contribution counter's design, reused: same
  flip-card geometry (71x92 at 83px, 16px gaps, 2px frame, the split line
  across each card), same brand fonts, same spacing-style contract. The number
  is the only thing that changes -- a countdown instead of
  `shop.metafields.custom.donation_total`.

  It is a COPY, not an edit. `sections/ona-donation-counter.liquid` and
  `assets/bfcm-countdown.js` are both untouched: WFG is coming back and the
  BFCM landing page has to keep rendering as it does today. The cost of the
  copy is that a geometry fix has to be made twice; the alternative was one
  section with a mode flag, which would have put campaign risk on the WFG
  asset during the WFG off-season. Not worth it.

  Two differences from the WFG original worth knowing:

  1. Cards hold TWO characters here, not one. A countdown unit is "07", and
     forcing it through the one-character card would have squashed the
     proportions, so `--bf-card-w` is the 71-wide slot doubled. The split line
     and the frame are unchanged.
  2. Every visible string is a setting, including the three countdown states.
     The WFG counter hard-codes its labels and `bfcm-countdown.js` hard-codes
     "Black Friday Cyber Monday is on"; neither is editable without a deploy,
     and this banner will have its wording changed more than once before the
     21st.

  SMS is NOT collected here, although the brief asks for it. `form 'customer'`
  creates an email subscriber; it does not establish SMS marketing consent, and
  a phone field that silently drops the number is worse than no field. Needs a
  Dotdigital (or SMS app) decision first -- see the PR.

  Dates default to the 21-27 November window Macarena confirmed, with the
  countdown pointed at early access on the 20th, because early access is what
  the sign-up is actually offering.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign start_at = section.settings.countdown_start_at | strip
  assign end_at = section.settings.countdown_end_at | strip
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  `spacing-style` is the class that defines --spacing-scale. The snippet emits
  `max(20px, calc(var(--spacing-scale) * Npx))` for any padding above 20px, so
  without the class every padding setting from 21 to 100 silently does nothing.
{%- endcomment -%}
<section
  class="bf-banner spacing-style"
  style="
    background-color: {{ section.settings.bg_color }};
    {% render 'spacing-style', settings: section.settings %}
    --bf-button-background: {{ section.settings.button_bg_color }};
    --bf-button-text: {{ section.settings.button_text_color }};
    --bf-card-gap: {{ section.settings.card_gap }}px;
    --bf-digit-size: {{ section.settings.digit_size }}px;
    --bf-digit-size-setting: {{ section.settings.digit_size }}px;
    --bf-heading-size: {{ section.settings.heading_size }}px;
    --bf-subtitle-size: {{ section.settings.subtitle_size }}px;
    --bf-heading-color: {{ section.settings.heading_color }};
    --bf-subtitle-color: {{ section.settings.subtitle_color }};
    --bf-card-bg: {{ section.settings.card_bg_color }};
    --bf-card-ink: {{ section.settings.card_ink_color }};
    --bf-frame-color: {{ section.settings.frame_color }};
  "
  {{ section.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <div class="bf-banner__inner">
    <bf-banner-countdown
      class="bf-banner__countdown"
      data-start-at="{{ start_at | escape }}"
      data-end-at="{{ end_at | escape }}"
      data-label-before="{{ section.settings.label_before | escape }}"
      data-label-live="{{ section.settings.label_live | escape }}"
      data-label-ended="{{ section.settings.label_ended | escape }}"
      data-text-live="{{ section.settings.text_live | escape }}"
      data-text-ended="{{ section.settings.text_ended | escape }}"
    >
      <span class="bf-banner__eyebrow" data-countdown-status>{{ section.settings.label_before }}</span>

      {%- if section.settings.title != blank -%}
        <h2 class="bf-banner__heading">{{ section.settings.title }}</h2>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Hidden until the script confirms both dates parse. A countdown that
        renders 00:00:00:00 on a broken date is worse than one that renders
        nothing, so the fallback line carries the dates in words.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div
        class="bf-banner__clock"
        role="timer"
        aria-live="off"
        aria-label="{{ section.settings.clock_label | escape }}"
        data-countdown-clock
        hidden
      >
        {%- comment -%}
          Written out rather than looped over `days,hours,minutes,seconds`. A loop
          emitting `data-countdown-{{ unit }}` is invisible to a static check, and
          these four attributes are exactly the ones whose absence makes the script
          return early and render nothing. Spelled out, a test can see them, which
          is also how sections/bfcm-landing.liquid does it.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="bf-banner__unit">
          <div class="bf-banner__cards">
            <div class="bf-banner__card"><span data-countdown-days>00</span></div>
          </div>
          <span class="bf-banner__unit-label">{{ section.settings.label_days }}</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bf-banner__separator" aria-hidden="true"><span>:</span></div>

        <div class="bf-banner__unit">
          <div class="bf-banner__cards">
            <div class="bf-banner__card"><span data-countdown-hours>00</span></div>
          </div>
          <span class="bf-banner__unit-label">{{ section.settings.label_hours }}</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bf-banner__separator" aria-hidden="true"><span>:</span></div>

        <div class="bf-banner__unit">
          <div class="bf-banner__cards">
            <div class="bf-banner__card"><span data-countdown-minutes>00</span></div>
          </div>
          <span class="bf-banner__unit-label">{{ section.settings.label_minutes }}</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bf-banner__separator" aria-hidden="true"><span>:</span></div>

        <div class="bf-banner__unit">
          <div class="bf-banner__cards">
            <div class="bf-banner__card"><span data-countdown-seconds>00</span></div>
          </div>
          <span class="bf-banner__unit-label">{{ section.settings.label_seconds }}</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="bf-banner__fallback" data-countdown-fallback>{{ section.settings.date_line }}</p>
    </bf-banner-countdown>

    {%- if section.settings.subtitle != blank -%}
      <p class="bf-banner__subtitle">{{ section.settings.subtitle }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      The tag is what makes the list usable afterwards: it is how we email
      exactly this group and hand the same group to Google and Meta. Keep it
      identical to the landing page's tag so the two surfaces build one list.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if section.settings.show_signup -%}
      <div class="bf-banner__signup">
        {%- form 'customer', class: 'bf-banner__form' -%}
          <input type="hidden" name="contact[tags]" value="{{ section.settings.signup_tag | escape }}">
          <label class="bf-banner__form-label" for="bf-banner-email-{{ section.id }}">
            {{- section.settings.signup_heading -}}
          </label>
          <div class="bf-banner__form-row">
            <input
              id="bf-banner-email-{{ section.id }}"
              type="email"
              name="contact[email]"
              placeholder="{{ section.settings.signup_placeholder | escape }}"
              autocomplete="email"
              required
              {% if form.errors %}
                aria-invalid="true"
                aria-describedby="bf-banner-error-{{ section.id }}"
              {% endif %}
            >
            <button type="submit">{{ section.settings.signup_button }}</button>
          </div>
          {%- if form.errors -%}
            <div id="bf-banner-error-{{ section.id }}" class="bf-banner__form-message" role="alert">
              {{- form.errors | default_errors -}}
            </div>
          {%- elsif form.posted_successfully? -%}
            <p class="bf-banner__form-message" role="status">{{ section.settings.signup_success }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endform -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.cta_text != blank and section.settings.cta_url != blank -%}
      <div class="bf-banner__actions">
        <a href="{{ section.settings.cta_url }}" class="button bf-banner__cta">
          {{- section.settings.cta_text -}}
        </a>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

<script src="{{ 'bf-banner-countdown.js' | asset_url }}" type="module"></script>

{% stylesheet %}
  .bf-banner {
    /* The four values come from the editor via spacing-style; the class on the
       section supplies both --spacing-scale and the 0px defaults it falls back
       to, so no literal fallback belongs here. */
    padding-block: var(--padding-block-start) var(--padding-block-end);
    padding-inline: var(--padding-inline-start) var(--padding-inline-end);
    text-align: center;
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  .bf-banner__inner {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .bf-banner__eyebrow {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-brand-text, 'Karla', sans-serif);
    font-size: var(--bf-subtitle-size, 16px);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--bf-subtitle-color, #fbf8f3);
  }

  .bf-banner__heading {
    font-family: var(--font-brand-display, 'Silk Serif', serif);
    font-size: var(--bf-heading-size, 40px);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin: 12px 0 24px;
    color: var(--bf-heading-color, #fbf8f3);
  }

  .bf-banner__clock {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--bf-card-gap, 16px);
  }

  /* `hidden` loses to `display: inline-flex` without this. */
  .bf-banner__clock[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .bf-banner__unit {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .bf-banner__cards {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    border: 2px solid var(--bf-frame-color, #000);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 13px 14px;
  }

  .bf-banner__card {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    /* The WFG card is a 71x92 slot at 83px for ONE character. A countdown unit
       is two characters, so the slot is doubled in width and the height and the
       split line are left exactly as they are. */
    width: calc(var(--bf-digit-size, 64px) * 142 / 83);
    height: calc(var(--bf-digit-size, 64px) * 92 / 83);
    background: var(--bf-card-bg, #f2f0eb);
    font-family: var(--font-brand-text, 'Karla', sans-serif);
    font-size: var(--bf-digit-size, 64px);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--bf-card-ink, #441925);
  }

  /* The split across the middle of each card -- it reads as a flip counter. */
  .bf-banner__card::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 0;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    width: 100%;
    height: 5px;
    background-color: var(--bf-card-ink, #441925);
    pointer-events: none;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .bf-banner__separator {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    /* Line the colon up with the middle of the cards, not the unit labels. */
    height: calc(var(--bf-digit-size, 64px) * 92 / 83 + 26px);
    font-family: var(--font-brand-text, 'Karla', sans-serif);
    font-size: calc(var(--bf-digit-size, 64px) * 0.6);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--bf-card-bg, #f2f0eb);
  }

  .bf-banner__unit-label {
    font-family: var(--font-brand-text, 'Karla', sans-serif);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--bf-subtitle-color, #fbf8f3);
  }

  .bf-banner__fallback {
    font-family: var(--font-brand-text, 'Karla', sans-serif);
    font-size: var(--bf-subtitle-size, 16px);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--bf-subtitle-color, #fbf8f3);
  }

  .bf-banner__fallback[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .bf-banner__subtitle {
    font-family: var(--font-brand-text, 'Karla', sans-serif);
    font-size: var(--bf-subtitle-size, 16px);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 24px auto 0;
    max-width: 48ch;
    color: var(--bf-subtitle-color, #fbf8f3);
  }

  .bf-banner__signup {
    margin-top: 28px;
  }

  .bf-banner__form {
    display: grid;
    gap: 9px;
    max-width: 460px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .bf-banner__form-label {
    font-family: var(--font-brand-text, 'Karla', sans-serif);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--bf-subtitle-color, #fbf8f3);
  }

  .bf-banner__form-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .bf-banner__form input {
    min-width: 0;
    flex: 1;
    min-height: 50px;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 0;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    background: var(--bf-card-bg, #f2f0eb);
    color: var(--bf-card-ink, #441925);
    font: inherit;
  }

  .bf-banner__form button {
    min-height: 50px;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 0;
    padding: 10px 22px;
    background: var(--bf-button-background, #f2f0eb);
    color: var(--bf-button-text, #441925);
    font: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .bf-banner__form-message {
    font-family: var(--font-brand-text, 'Karla', sans-serif);
    font-size: 13px;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--bf-subtitle-color, #fbf8f3);
  }

  .bf-banner__actions {
    margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .bf-banner__cta {
    background: var(--bf-button-background, #f2f0eb);
    color: var(--bf-button-text, #441925);
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    /* Mobile redefines the BASE size and lets the proportional rules above do
       the work, rather than scaling each one by a constant. A constant cannot
       know the viewport: at the 64px default a flat 0.62 asks for roughly
       429px of clock (four 68px cards, each inside 18px of padding and a 4px
       frame, plus six gaps and three colons) inside the 335px a 375px phone
       leaves after this section's 20px inline padding -- it overflowed the
       page. Driving it from `vw` makes the fit a property of the layout
       instead of a number someone has to re-check.

       Capped by `--bf-digit-size-setting` as well as by 40px, so choosing a
       size SMALLER than the cap is still honoured here; only oversized values
       are clamped down to what the screen can hold. */
    .bf-banner__clock {
      --bf-digit-size: clamp(22px, 7vw, min(40px, var(--bf-digit-size-setting, 64px)));
      gap: clamp(4px, 1.6vw, calc(var(--bf-card-gap, 16px) / 2));
      max-width: 100%;
    }

    .bf-banner__cards {
      padding: 6px 7px;
    }

    .bf-banner__unit {
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .bf-banner__unit-label {
      font-size: 10px;
    }

    .bf-banner__separator {
      /* Vertical padding (6px x 2) plus the 2px frame, matching the cards. */
      height: calc(var(--bf-digit-size, 64px) * 92 / 83 + 16px);
      font-size: calc(var(--bf-digit-size, 64px) * 0.5);
    }

    .bf-banner__form-row {
      flex-direction: column;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "BF countdown banner",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "title",
      "label": "Title",
      "default": "Black Friday"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "subtitle",
      "label": "Subtitle",
      "default": "Seven days of our best coffee. Subscribers see it first."
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "bg_color",
      "label": "Background color",
      "default": "#441925"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Countdown"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "countdown_start_at",
      "label": "Countdown start (ISO 8601)",
      "default": "2026-11-20T00:00:00+11:00",
      "info": "Early access opens. Needs a full date, time AND offset for Sydney, e.g. 2026-11-20T00:00:00+11:00 — without the offset the clock is wrong by the viewer's timezone and will not render at all."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "countdown_end_at",
      "label": "Countdown end (ISO 8601)",
      "default": "2026-11-28T00:00:00+11:00",
      "info": "End of the sale. After this the banner shows the ended wording."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "date_line",
      "label": "Date line (shown instead of the clock)",
      "default": "21–27 November 2026",
      "info": "Also the fallback if either date above is malformed."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label_before",
      "label": "Label before it starts",
      "default": "Early access opens in"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label_live",
      "label": "Label while it is on",
      "default": "Black Friday is on"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label_ended",
      "label": "Label after it ends",
      "default": "That is a wrap"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "text_live",
      "label": "Line while it is on",
      "default": "Shop now — ends Friday 27 November."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "text_ended",
      "label": "Line after it ends",
      "default": "Join the list to hear first next time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label_days",
      "label": "Unit label: days",
      "default": "Days"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label_hours",
      "label": "Unit label: hours",
      "default": "Hours"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label_minutes",
      "label": "Unit label: minutes",
      "default": "Mins"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label_seconds",
      "label": "Unit label: seconds",
      "default": "Secs"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "clock_label",
      "label": "Screen reader label for the clock",
      "default": "Time until Black Friday early access"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Sign up"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_signup",
      "label": "Show the sign-up form",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "signup_heading",
      "label": "Sign-up heading",
      "default": "Sign up for early access, offers and every update."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "signup_placeholder",
      "label": "Email placeholder",
      "default": "Email address"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "signup_button",
      "label": "Button text",
      "default": "Sign up"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "signup_success",
      "label": "Success message",
      "default": "You are on the list. We will email you first."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "signup_tag",
      "label": "Customer tag",
      "default": "BFCM 2026",
      "info": "Must match the landing page tag so both surfaces build one list."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Link"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cta_text",
      "label": "Link text",
      "default": "See the sale"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "cta_url",
      "label": "Link url"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Colours"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "heading_color",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "#fbf8f3"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "subtitle_color",
      "label": "Subtitle and labels",
